A||||5||Kelvin Vivian||SPIN story||||1||
Z||000000||Kelvin Vivian||04-01-2001||03:10 AM||||What's your best (or worst) spinout in a Fiero?<P>Here's mine, 2 years ago in Southern CA:<P>I'm stopped at a red light on Wilshire Ave. The 270 degree freeway onramp to the 405 freeway is about 75-100 yards ahead. I need to be in the lane to the right of me so that I can get onto the freeway. Problem - there is a large 454 V8 Chevy pickup to my right, I'm in a 85 SE 4-cyl 5-spd. As we were waiting at the light I just happen to notice that there is a white Mercedes S600 V-12 in the lane to the left of me, it was a nice car. But I quickly dismiss the V-12 Mercedes because I must beat the 454 V8 chevy so that I can get onto the freeway!!!<P>Concentrate, concentrate, light turns green, and I punch it! I get the jump on 454 V8 and merge into the right lane, I look in the rear view and the V12 Merc is behind me!!! V12 Merc must have been trying to get the jump on both me and the 454 V8....<P>Problem #2 - there was a light rain, and I didn't really have too much time to slow down my onramp entry speed... As I'm braking, and turning, the back end of the Fiero slowly spins around, and I'm facing V12... V12 saw the whole thing and stopped the traffic behind him, I flipped a quick U and merged onto the freeway...||||reg||1
Z||000001||danny boy||04-01-2001||03:27 AM|||| Been awhile. This was pre GT days. I was in my 86 4cyl/5sp. taking a friend for a ride. He had a VW Scirroco16V andNeither one of us had driven our cars for about six months. I got mine back on the road first. After all the talk about how good it handled(it acually did)I had to impress.We leave town and head out old Cheat road.This road is the windiest(sp?) road I could think of that would still be fast enough to be fun.<BR> We're running along at a decent clip when we get to the last turn before the lake. I'm doing about sixty as I come out of the next to last turn and hit the small straight. He mutters "big turn" while I'm still picking up speed."Big turn" a little louder. We're doind 75."BIG TURN!" too late. I mash the brakes to slow down and catch the apex just right but we all know what happens when a Fiero goes into a turn too fast and then the driver gets on the brakes to whoa it down. "Hold on, we're goin' around" I tell him.Sure enough, we end up looking at the turn we just came out of and WHAM! guardrail.<BR>Bounce once, bounce twice, then get away from it but get stuck in the gravel on the berm.Both of us are just staring out the windshield, waiting for the dust to settle. We get out, survey the damage and.... just a little less paint.||||reg||1
Z||000002||danny boy||04-01-2001||03:29 AM||||   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/red_car_pics.jpg">  <BR> this was the morning before.<p>[This message has been edited by danny boy (edited 04-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||KnightRyder31||04-01-2001||09:03 AM||||Never spun out before, unless it was on purpose.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tina||04-01-2001||10:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Kelvin Vivian:<BR><B>What's your  worst spinout in a Fiero?<BR>Problem - there was a light rain...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Bring back some memories  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Right turn lane- Red Light- Attempt to <BR> turn on to 2 lane street.<P>Too lazy for 1st gear, so let the clutch up in second.<BR>Roar, then slip slide,this is the mother of all fishtails.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> I'am in the left lane,<BR>No the right,no back in the left. <BR>Ahhhh, the median.<BR>Uhhh, back in the right. (Deep breath)<BR>Thank god,I had a few feet of room in front <BR>and back.<P>Mental note: Next time you get new tires, road test 'em on empty street.<BR>Or call sister in germany for test report<BR>on tires.<BR>(Yokohama got a failing grade due to behavior<BR>on wet roads)<BR>BTW I hate it, when I get a "Told you so " from the little sis.<P>Tina<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||04-01-2001||05:08 PM||||Start of this winter... our first snow, really wet and slushy.  225/60 15 BFG TA's on the back without much tread.. coming home from my g/f's house, the highway was clear so i was doing about 50.  Get to my exit, see that there's about 1-2 inches of pure slush on it.  Try to slow down.. as soon as I hit the slush the back end spins to the right, straight for the grass.  I stare through the passenger window at the marker sign that I'm heading straight for..  &lt;wham!&gt; snapped the sign clear off, it took out most of my pass. side ground f/x, bent the mirror and tore the fender from the splash shield... i was pissed.  There's a thread about it somewhere here...||||reg||1
